
c)	Write a simple "Hello World" application using Spring

Aim: To create a simple "Hello World" application using Spring Boot.

Procedure:
1.	Create a Spring Boot project using Spring Initializr
2.	Add dependency: Spring Web
3.	Open the project in IDE (VS Code / IntelliJ)
4.	Create a controller class
5.	Run the application

Main Class:
package com.example.demo;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;

@SpringBootApplication
public class DemoApplication {
public static void main(String[] args) {
SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);
}
}
Hello World Controller:
package com.example.demo;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

@RestController
public class HelloController {
@GetMapping("/hello")
public String hello() {
return "Hello World using Spring Boot!";
}
}

How to Run:
•	Run DemoApplication.java
•	Open browser

URL:
http://localhost:8080/hello

Output:
Hello World using Spring Boot!
 
